# GDD Russian mirror

English files under `docs/gdd/*.md` are canonical. Do not create, update, or delete Russian mirrors (`<Name> - RU.md`) unless the user explicitly asks for a Russian translation or for the mirrors to be synced.

- A GDD edit is done when the English file is updated. Stale or missing RU files are not a blocker.
- If the user does ask for a RU mirror: same sections, same facts, same checklist states; English wins on disagreement; Cyrillic is allowed in RU files, but punctuation stays plain ASCII (`"` not `«»`, `-` not `—`, `...` not `…`).
- Never change a RU mirror without the matching English change.
- Every RU file carries its source as the first line: `<!-- source: <commit> -->`, the repo commit holding the English text it was translated from. For files synced from core (`docs/gdd/National Focuses - RU.md`), the line names the core commit and is byte-identical in all repos so the sync stays green.
- Translate incrementally: when the English file moves, diff it against the recorded commit (`git show <hash>:<path>` or `git log <hash>..HEAD -- <path>`), translate only the changed sections, then point the source line at the new HEAD. Never re-translate a whole doc for a small English edit.
- `.scratch/scripts/check_ru_mirror.py <EN> <RU>` verifies sections, checkboxes, punctuation and source freshness; a stale source line fails the check. Run it after every mirror touch. A source hash unknown to the mod repo but present in its `core` submodule means a synced file: freshness is then owned by core (and drift by the sync check), so the mirror check defers with a note instead of failing.
